00:34:37,240 --> 00:34:37,760
I'm sorry, John.

385
00:34:37,760 --> 00:34:39,220
I'm sitting next to you.

386
00:34:39,220 --> 00:34:39,500
No, right.

387
00:34:39,520 --> 00:34:40,640
Sorry, it'll steal my thunder.

388
00:34:41,960 --> 00:34:42,580
Yeah, go ahead.

389
00:34:43,240 --> 00:34:47,320
No, I find it very interesting, and I appreciate your words on this.

390
00:34:49,600 --> 00:34:52,140
It's a lot of wells, right?

391
00:34:52,840 --> 00:34:58,060
I guess originally I did not realize that it was individual wells per unit.

392
00:34:58,520 --> 00:35:00,240
Individual wells, individual septic.

393
00:35:00,240 --> 00:35:00,900
It's not some wells, right?

394
00:35:01,060 --> 00:35:02,940
It's 21.

395
00:35:03,500 --> 00:35:03,880
21.

396
00:35:04,060 --> 00:35:04,400
21.

397
00:35:04,840 --> 00:35:07,920
Yeah, 21 units, 21 wells, 21 septics.

398
00:35:08,060 --> 00:35:08,760
That's a lot of money.

399
00:35:09,100 --> 00:35:09,980
Not many acres.

400
00:35:09,980 --> 00:35:14,240
And then I am concerned about the buffer.

401
00:35:15,440 --> 00:35:26,720
One of the things I guess that I don't like about the buffer is that it's assuming that we would approve the intrusion into it.

402
00:35:26,720 --> 00:35:29,060
These plans were drawn in that way.

403
00:35:31,160 --> 00:35:33,480
It's kind of a big assumption, right?

404
00:35:34,080 --> 00:35:37,460
It's kind of throwing the point of the buffer away.

405
00:35:37,920 --> 00:35:42,580
You know, this whole thing was drawn on an assumption.

406
00:35:42,580 --> 00:35:54,780
And if you look at where, you know, some of these wells are right on the edge, on the opposite edge of the 50-foot buffer, they're not on the inside edge.

407
00:35:55,100 --> 00:35:57,960
And it is aggressive topography.

408
00:35:58,240 --> 00:36:03,620
You're going to need, I don't know, I mean, you've got to get a well truck in there.

409
00:36:04,560 --> 00:36:08,400
You're not talking about disturbing a little bit of path.

410
00:36:09,600 --> 00:36:10,800
You've got to get a rig in there.

411
00:36:13,060 --> 00:36:18,240
You'd like to see if there's some system they can install that's not going to get all those wells in the buffer?

412
00:36:18,480 --> 00:36:24,220
Yeah, I mean, it's interesting, I guess, as we think about this, like, why we didn't do, like, a community well.

413
00:36:24,620 --> 00:36:25,660
Like, why wouldn't that be?

414
00:36:26,840 --> 00:36:33,300
Again, I mean, that's what, for starters, like I said, the owners wanted individual septics and wells.

415
00:36:33,620 --> 00:36:36,700
For that reason, maybe you could even ask them, because they're in the audience.

416
00:36:36,880 --> 00:36:45,680
But a community water system, even though you're drilling, potentially has the expense of being even greater than drilling 21 wells.

417
00:36:46,280 --> 00:36:52,340
And costs them a lot of time getting the approvals for the community water system stuff as well.

418
00:36:52,340 --> 00:36:59,220
So it's, and I don't need to re-explain to the board that this has been before the board for a long, long, long time.

