957
01:07:21,340 --> 01:07:25,340
Mark Caledaria waiver is respectfully, uh, requested from section 923.

958
01:07:25,340 --> 01:07:31,340
The town is saying down subdivision regulations requiring the provision of onsite recreational facilities.

959
01:07:31,340 --> 01:07:35,340
The proposed subdivision will create one new residential lot.

960
01:07:35,340 --> 01:07:42,340
Providing recreational facilities within these private residential lots would offer little or no practical benefit to the general public.

961
01:07:42,340 --> 01:07:53,340
The property is accessed from a class six road, uh, that is not maintained by the town and is not readily, uh, accessible or appropriate for public, uh, recreational use.

962
01:07:53,340 --> 01:08:05,340
Establishing a public or shared recreational area in this location would also create unnecessary access, maintenance, security, and liability concerns for the future private, um, property owners.

963
01:08:05,340 --> 01:08:16,340
Strict compliance with section 923 would therefore not accomplish the regulations and intended public purpose under the particular conditions of this property.

964
01:08:16,340 --> 01:08:35,340
A voluntary, uh, contribution to the town of Sandown's recreation, recreation revolving fund would provide a more practical and meaningful public benefit by allowing the town to apply the funds towards recreational facilities that are appropriately located publicly accessible and maintained for public use.

965
01:08:35,340 --> 01:08:49,340
Accordingly, the applicant proposes a voluntary contribution of $1,000 for the one new residential lot created by the subdivision, um, the contribution would be paid at the time of a certificate of occupancy is issued for the new dwelling.

966
01:08:49,340 --> 01:08:53,340
The existing lot and dwelling would not be subject to any additional contribution.

967
01:08:53,340 --> 01:09:04,340
Um, granting this waiver would remain consistent with the spirit and intent of the subdivision regulations would not be contrary to the public interest and would provide a more effective recreational benefit to the town.

968
01:09:04,340 --> 01:09:10,340
than requiring an isolated recreational area on private property access by a classics road.

969
01:09:10,340 --> 01:09:17,340
For these reasons, the applicant respectfully request the planning board approve the waiver from section 923 signed to me.

